# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): a deferred record's phase
# (`Deferred::phase`, sys/cgroup.rs) is written only through these
# wrappers, which no other file calls but heap/slotstate.rs's `step` (the
# slot-state bytes, whose permission `axiom_slot_byte` mints there), and
# this file mints one BytePerm per atomic, in `new`
# (tests/loom/tests/access.rs). C++20's coherence
# rules ([intro.races]) give a load the permission's value at its place in
# the byte's modification order; the exchange is a read-modify-write,
# which reads the last value for every ordering ([atomics.order] p10), in
# the strong form, which fails only when the values differ; and the
# `Release` store of `DONE` with an `Acquire` load or exchange that reads
# it orders the record's plain writes before its readers (a
# release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2). The oncecell models check
# that hand-off and the fork child's reset on copies of the `Deferred`
# steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The GenMC slotstate case runs
# `compare_exchange` as it is, with the permission erased, on the slot
# state byte's free step only (tests/genmc/slotstate.rs); no case runs the
# `Deferred` steps or `load` and `store`.
load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::byte_load, and loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_discover_races_get and oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_fork_child_restarts; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Deferred` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states; the C11 argument above that the permission's value is the phase's last write, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 4086422618, body 2728638763
store	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::byte_store, and loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_discover_races_get and oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_fork_child_restarts; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Deferred` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states; the C11 argument above, which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3007128824, body 3208554845
compare_exchange	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::byte_compare_exchange, and loom: oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_discover_races_get and oncecell::loom_oncecell_deferred_fork_child_restarts, and GenMC: slotstate [rc11 imm]; not checked: this body under concurrency beyond the part of C11 loom models (stale `Relaxed` and `Acquire` loads within a bounded store history, and no load buffering, as verus/WEAKMEM.md states), which the models run as it is over loom's atomic inside copies of the `Deferred` steps, in the configurations tests/loom/src/oncecell.rs states, and beyond the configuration tests/genmc/slotstate.rs states, which the GenMC case runs it in as it is over `core`'s atomic on a slot's state byte (`slotstate::step`'s call), not on the `Deferred` phase, under RC11 and IMM only (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC": the `-Copt-level=1` IR, not the release build); the value a failed exchange returns, a load's; that it never fails spuriously, which neither loom's nor GenMC's compare-and-swap can show and rests on `core`'s documentation of the strong form; the C11 argument above, which no GenMC case checks (the case erases the permission, `Tracked::assume_new()`, so it sees no ghost value) and tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text only)	contract 3457651930, body 129076834
